      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Python chat validator (`check_logprobs` in `vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py`) requires `logprobs=true` only when `top_logprobs` is `-1` or positive, so `top_logprobs: 0` (the OpenAI default) is accepted on its own. The Rust frontend rejects any `top_logprobs` without `logprobs`, so clients and SDKs that always send `top_logprobs: 0` get a 400 that Python would not return. This PR applies Python's condition in the Rust chat checks.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `POST /v1/chat/completions` with `top_logprobs: 0` and no `logprobs` now returns 200 on the Rust frontend, matching Python.\n- `top_logprobs: 1` or `-1` without `logprobs` is still rejected with 400.\n\nWithout `logprobs`:\n\n| `top_logprobs` | Python | Rust before | Rust after |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `0` | 200 | 400 | 200 |\n| `1` or `-1` | 400 | 400 | 400 |\n\n## Validation\n\nCommands from `.buildkite/scripts/run-rust-frontend-cargo-ci.sh` (`style-clippy` and `test`), run from the repo root:\n\n```\ncargo fmt --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml --all -- --check   # ok\ncargo sort --workspace --check rust                          # ok\ncargo deny --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml --config rust/deny.toml check bans   # ok\ncargo clippy --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings   # ok\ncargo nextest run --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml --workspace --all-features --locked --no-fail-fast\n# 2140 tests run: 2140 passed, 13 skipped\n```\n\nThe new `validate_request_compat_accepts_zero_top_logprobs_without_logprobs` fails on the base (checked by reverting only the two conditions). The existing rejection test now covers `-1` and `1` through both the schema validator and `validate_request_compat`.\n\n## Details\n\nThe Rust frontend has two checks for this dependency, and both are changed in place: the schema validator (`validate_chat_cross_parameters` in `chat_completions/types.rs`), which runs first in `ValidatedJson`, and `validate_request_compat` in `chat_completions/validate.rs`, which runs during request preparation. They duplicate each other; merging them is out of scope here.\n\nNot a duplicate: open upstream PRs touching `top_logprobs` in the Rust frontend (vllm-project/vllm#58711, vllm-project/vllm#60916) change logprob output and raw generate, not this request validation.\n\nAI assistance (Claude Code) was used to prepare this change; the human submitter reviewed every changed line.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
